{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9412-agenda-conditions","id":9412,"title":"Agenda Conditions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-12T19:43:49-08:00","id":9412,"title":"Agenda Conditions?","content":"Are they a one time thing? If not, how do you regain them?<br /> <br /> I'm loving everything I'm reading so far, you guys are getting my money for the KS!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T19:47:20-08:00","id":9415,"title":"","content":"You get them back at the beginning of a chapter (session), pp. 126-127, so you do best to fulfill the beat prerequisite and then resolve the condition every session, beat-wise. Or resolve them twice, if you have Consummate Professional \u2022\u2022!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:01:17-08:00","id":9842,"title":"","content":"From: Integrators<br /> <br /> &quot;Beat: Take a Beat when the character puts the ring at risk or makes the ring vocally or actively suspicious of his motives.&quot;<br /> <br /> So am I misreading this or on a functional level (aside from their belief systems being valid or invalid) is this agenda going to be obscenely attractive to players who just want to troll their Ring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:21:28-08:00","id":9859,"title":"","content":"Probably. <br /> <br /> Real talk: <b>Demon</b> is written with the assumption that the players at the table are on the same page, that everyone is trying to play the same game, that the Storyteller has communicated the expectations properly, and that no one is actively being a gigantic fuckhammer. I got tired of writing &quot;balanced&quot; mechanics (where &quot;balanced&quot; means &quot;written from the assumptions that the players are giggling assholes&quot;) around the year 2001 or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:38:47-08:00","id":9871,"title":"","content":"Awesome. This right here is why I am a fervent supporter of WW/OP vs. Others <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:45:48-08:00","id":9994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9412-agenda-conditions?p=9859#post9859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably.<br /> <br /> Real talk: <b>Demon</b> is written with the assumption that the players at the table are on the same page, that everyone is trying to play the same game, that the Storyteller has communicated the expectations properly, and that no one is actively being a gigantic fuckhammer. I got tired of writing &quot;balanced&quot; mechanics (where &quot;balanced&quot; means &quot;written from the assumptions that the players are giggling assholes&quot;) around the year 2001 or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for this. I now have a quote to explain why game design can't be based on the actions of jerks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampir